<title>RUSSIA: Russia details 1996 sugar, coffee, cocoa imports.</title>
<headline>Russia details 1996 sugar, coffee, cocoa imports.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia imported 1.70 million tonnes of raw sugar from all destinations in 1996, a 35 percent jump from the 1.25 million imported in 1995, the State Statistics Committee said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The data, as reported by Interfax news agency, showed white sugar imports fell over the same period to 1.44 million tonnes from 1.78 million.</p>
<p>Russia imported 55,900 tonnes of cocoa beans last year, little changed from the 56,300 imported in 1995.</p>
<p>Coffee imports slipped slightly to 25,000 tonnes from 26,000 in 1995.</p>
<p>The committee issued the following data for soft commodity imports from all destinations--</p>
<p>	 RUSSIAN IMPORTS OF SUGAR, COFFEE AND COCOA</p>
<p>			     (tonnes)</p>
<p>				    1996	     1995</p>
<p> Sugar (raw)		 1,696,100	1,251,900</p>
<p> Sugar (refined)	   1,441,600	1,781,000</p>
<p> Cocoa			    55,900	   56,300</p>
<p> Coffee			   25,000	   26,000</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom +095 941 8520</p>
</text>
